                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e470c0aa-85ca-3a22-92a4-b0a23806e93e",
                        "entry_id": "a848b635-2261-34de-98ff-b30133e41edf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "то же, что заключённый"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3767ee00-4c2c-498c-bf72-56e139164474",
                                "sense_id": "e470c0aa-85ca-3a22-92a4-b0a23806e93e",
                                "text": "Редкий зэк не побывал на трёх-пяти пересылках, многие припомнят с десяток их, а сыны ГУЛага начтут без труда и полусотню."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c0c5803-177b-4033-8e53-85f3799952ce",
                                "sense_id": "e470c0aa-85ca-3a22-92a4-b0a23806e93e",
                                "text": "Зэки плохо представляют, что ждёт их на воле."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fdb26639-58e3-4cf3-aee8-3acf1e178eab",
                        "source_entry_id": "a848b635-2261-34de-98ff-b30133e41edf",
                        "source_sense_id": "e470c0aa-85ca-3a22-92a4-b0a23806e93e",
                        "target_lang_word": "prisoner",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "prisoner",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7341d926-2e89-3a36-acb9-7316b94f38cb",
                                        "entry_id": "8f96aade-77bc-3b07-88f0-f1fd0fdf570f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person incarcerated in a prison, while on trial or serving a sentence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83f9c94c-e1e7-45d9-9bda-a7d925cc66c2",
                                                "sense_id": "7341d926-2e89-3a36-acb9-7316b94f38cb",
                                                "text": "Two other prisoners were staying in the same cell as him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecff8481-0a8a-4356-b99c-a0587a2c82a2",
                                                "sense_id": "7341d926-2e89-3a36-acb9-7316b94f38cb",
                                                "text": "The evidence disclosed that the three prisoners were in a public-house together with the prosecutor, Abraham Rhodes, and that in concert with the other two prisoners, the prisoner John Dewhirst placed a pencase on the table in the room where they were assembled, and left the room to get writing-paper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a897d78-9989-460d-b0ce-d4b047eff474",
                                                "sense_id": "7341d926-2e89-3a36-acb9-7316b94f38cb",
                                                "text": "American journalist Evan Gershkovich and former US Marine Paul Whelan were among the 24 detainees released as part of a complex prisoner swap between Russia, the US and other Western nations. […] Krasikov, a former high-ranking FSB colonel serving a life sentence in a German prison, was on the top of Moscow’s list of Russian prisoners it wanted to exchange."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45feebf1-469c-36bb-bb3f-e35dd0cde2dc",
                                        "entry_id": "8f96aade-77bc-3b07-88f0-f1fd0fdf570f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any person held against their will."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fed10d49-3a6d-461c-93e6-211ea5090a5f",
                                                "sense_id": "45feebf1-469c-36bb-bb3f-e35dd0cde2dc",
                                                "text": "And gainſt the General we will lift our ſwords / And either lanch his greedie thirſting throat, / Or take him priſoner, and his chaine ſhall ſerue / For Manackles, till he be ranſom’d home."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27825753-244a-408d-8e27-06acaa6eed23",
                                                "sense_id": "45feebf1-469c-36bb-bb3f-e35dd0cde2dc",
                                                "text": "Captain Edward Carlisle, soldier as he was, martinet as he was, felt a curious sensation of helplessness seize upon him as he met her steady gaze, her alluring smile ; he could not tell what this prisoner might do."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "757e2260-9716-315b-a96a-763935d6170d",
                                        "entry_id": "8f96aade-77bc-3b07-88f0-f1fd0fdf570f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who is or feels confined or trapped by a situation or a set of circumstances."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6eabbee-6245-4ea3-b0b6-07ce02fdda7d",
                                                "sense_id": "757e2260-9716-315b-a96a-763935d6170d",
                                                "text": "I am no longer a prisoner to fear, for I am a child of God."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0a062008-0edc-477a-be30-7510ee13038d",
                        "source_entry_id": "a848b635-2261-34de-98ff-b30133e41edf",
                        "source_sense_id": "e470c0aa-85ca-3a22-92a4-b0a23806e93e",
                        "target_lang_word": "convict",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "convict",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a3cd14d-3c5c-39b4-9ff1-87ecca6b86e9",
                                        "entry_id": "69fd70c4-6788-30e6-b32a-b19af91dd3ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To find guilty, as a result of legal proceedings, or (informal) in a moral sense."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6de27130-cf5e-4d26-8d2a-22565ae0c705",
                                                "sense_id": "7a3cd14d-3c5c-39b4-9ff1-87ecca6b86e9",
                                                "text": "His remarks convicted him of a lack of sensitivity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdd58254-af30-42fe-a99e-ac876807df38",
                                                "sense_id": "7a3cd14d-3c5c-39b4-9ff1-87ecca6b86e9",
                                                "text": "He was a convicted felon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a379774-0edd-444e-b193-5dc4174b3259",
                                                "sense_id": "7a3cd14d-3c5c-39b4-9ff1-87ecca6b86e9",
                                                "text": "And his subjects wrung all they could wring / Out of temple and palace and store. / But when there seemed no more to bring, / His captors convicted the king / Of once having started a war, / And strangled the wretch with a string."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f1e9228-6225-3f90-a5a7-898de68bed6a",
                                        "entry_id": "69fd70c4-6788-30e6-b32a-b19af91dd3ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To convince, persuade; to cause (someone) to believe in (something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0f8711f-fbf3-41d8-ac84-b79fba8ff442",
                                                "sense_id": "8f1e9228-6225-3f90-a5a7-898de68bed6a",
                                                "text": "Rivian CEO RJ Scaringe is standing by his decision not to integrate Apple’s CarPlay into the company’s EVs, even as rivals embrace it. […] Speaking on The Verge’s Decoder podcast, Scaringe said Rivian aims to build a “seamless digital experience” entirely within its own software ecosystem. This means that Rivian will simply be offering native access to key apps like Apple Music, Spotify, Google Maps, and YouTube, according to MacRumors. […] Rivian’s software approach mirrors that of Tesla, which also relies on its own app integrations rather than Apple’s. […] The Rivian CEO added that the company is preparing to introduce AI-powered features within 18 months, including native voice-to-text messaging. Scaringe said this upcoming AI suite will further justify the brand’s decision to control the in-vehicle experience. “We’re really convicted on this,” the CEO said. While he acknowledged that some customers may avoid Rivian due to the lack of CarPlay, Scaringe said he’s “very confident” in the choice. “Some of those decisions not everyone’s going to agree with,” he said. “That’s okay.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "convict",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a08535c-1b09-3d6c-9079-831fbcdf30b5",
                                        "entry_id": "ec937467-2c29-3b76-bba6-f1ac5b365927",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person convicted of a crime by a judicial body."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae699b86-63f4-3173-9718-315ed81cdcab",
